writes': [], 'parent_id': '951908887332810812', 'nsfw': False, 'name': 'tarkov', 'last_message_id': '1219824218573766707', 'id': '1063511322307858484', 'icon_emoji': {'name': '🔫', 'id': None}, 'flags': 0}, {'version': 1774716996957, 'type': 0, 'topic': None, 'theme_color': None, 'rate_limit_per_user': 0, 'position': 5, 'permission_overwrites': [], 'parent_id': '951908887332810812', 'nsfw': False, 'name': 'music', 'last_pin_timestamp': '2024-10-02T00:38:48+00:00', 'last_message_id': '1437861090074558665', 'id': '1091945480210108458', 'icon_emoji': {'name': '🎵', 'id': None}, 'flags': 0}, {'version': 1774717004318, 'type': 0, 'topic': "To be fair, you have to have a very high speed to understand Sonic the Hedgehog. The gameplay is extremely fast, and without a solid grasp of platforming physics most of the levels will be impossible to complete. There's also Sonic's cool attitude, which is deftly woven into his characterisation - his personal philosophy draws heavily from the pop culture of the 90s, for instance. The fans understand this stuff; they have the reflexes to truly appreciate the depths of these games, to realise that they're not just fun - they say something deep about SPEED. As a consequence, people who dislike Sonic the Hedgehog truly ARE slow - of course they wouldn't appreciate, for instance, the rush of completing Green Hill Zone in under a minute, which itself is a cryptic reference to classic Sonic gameplay. I'm smirking right now just imagining one of those lagging slowpokes trying to keep up with me as I blaze through a Sonic game. What fools... how I pity them. :joy: And yes, by the way, I DO have a Sonic the Hedgehog t", 'theme_color': None, 'rate_limit_per_user': 0, 'position': 11, 'permission_overwrites': [], 'parent_id': '951908887332810812', 'nsfw': False, 'name': 'sonic-roleplay', 'last_message_id': '1504913847507484815', 'id': '1100833070405394503', 'icon_emoji': {'name': '🎮', 'id': None}, 'flags': 0}], 'emojis': [{'version': 1679936911581, 